{"summary":"Restore correct hexadecimal digit conversion","explanation":"The regression changes the adjustment for alphabetic hex digits from 9 to 8. That shifts A–F and a–f down by one, corrupting decoded bytes and Unicode values and causing the reported unescape failures. Restoring the original adjustment fixes the shared decoding path.","edits":[{"path":"absl/strings/escaping.cc","old":"  if (x > '9') {
    x += 8;
  }","new":"  if (x > '9') {
    x += 9;
  }"}]}
